+SERENA MCP TOOLS BRIEFING (ADHD-Optimized Code Intelligence)
+================================================================
+Serena v2 MCP Server provides 15 ADHD-optimized code intelligence tools.
+
+AVAILABLE TOOLS:
+- get_workspace_status()          : Check server health and workspace info
+- list_dir(relative_path)         : List directory contents
+- read_file(relative_path, lines)  : Read file content with line range
+- find_symbol(query, type, limit) : Search for symbols (max 10 results)
+- goto_definition(file, line, col): Navigate to definitions with context
+- find_references(file, line, col): Find all symbol references
+- analyze_complexity(file)        : Assess code complexity (0.0-1.0 scale)
+- filter_by_focus(state, items)   : Filter results by attention state
+- suggest_next_step(current_file) : Get navigation suggestions (max 3)
+- get_reading_order(files)        : Optimal reading sequence by complexity
+- detect_untracked_work()        : Feature 1 - Untracked work detection
+- update_focus_mode(mode)         : Set focus state (focused/scattered/transitioning)
+- find_relationships(symbol)      : Discover code dependencies
+- get_navigation_patterns()      : Navigation history analysis
+- get_context(file, line)         : Get surrounding code with context
+
+ADHD OPTIMIZATIONS:
+- Max 10 results everywhere to prevent overwhelm
+- Progressive disclosure (3-7 line contexts, not full files)
+- Complexity-based reading time estimates
+- Decision reduction (max 3 suggestions)
+- Graceful degradation when components unavailable
+- All tools respond in <200ms (ADHD performance target)
+
+USAGE EXAMPLES:
+# Initialize client
+from services.serena.mcp_client import create_mcp_client
+client = await create_mcp_client('http://localhost:3006')
+
+# Search for functions
+functions = await client.call_tool('find_symbol', {
